## The question to answer

{{ concept.canonical_question }}

Answer that question and only that question. It is the one the learner asked.

## Required content

The script must cover all five beats, in this order, one per scene:

{% for beat in concept.beats -%}
- **{{ beat.id }}** — {{ beat.content }}
{% endfor %}

{% if concept.narrative_shape == "causal" -%}
The question asks **why**, not what. Describing what the thing *is* — however
accurately — answers a different question. Beat B3 is where the "why" lives:
state plainly that the bonded arrangement is lower in energy, and therefore
more stable, than the separate atoms. A script without that has not answered
the question.
{%- elif concept.narrative_shape == "comparative" -%}
This is a **comparison**, not two explanations placed side by side. Every
scene from B1 onwards must address both sides on a single axis: state what
one does, then what the other does about the same thing. Explaining one type
fully and then the other is the most common way this goes wrong.
{%- else -%}
This is a **linear** explanation: each scene builds on the one before, from
what the quantity measures through to what it means in practice.
{%- endif %}

